# PR and branch flow

Canonical docs: `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `doc/setup/pr-and-merge-flow.md`, `.github/pull_request_template.md`.

## Topology (never skip hops)

```text
feature/* | fix/* | chore/* | …  →  dev  →  staging  →  main
```

| PR type | Base ← Head |
| --- | --- |
| Feature / fix | `dev` ← work branch |
| QA promotion | `staging` ← `dev` |
| Production promotion | `main` ← `staging` |

- Never open a feature PR into `main` or `staging`.
- Never push straight to `dev` / `staging` / `main`.
- Branch from latest `dev`.

## Reviews — English only

- Write **all PR reviews, review comments, and approval summaries in English**.
- PR titles/bodies may follow the template; prefer English for team-wide clarity.
- When posting reviews via `gh`, use English.

## Self-merge

- **Non-admins:** do not merge your own PR.
- **Repo/org admins:** may self-merge when needed (prefer a second reviewer for `staging` → `main`).

## Before asking for review

1. Fill the PR template (summary, ticket, target-branch checkboxes, checklist).
2. Run locally: `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test`.
3. Request at least one reviewer (CODEOWNERS may auto-request).

## Agent behavior

- When creating/updating PRs: target the correct base; never suggest `feature → main`.
- When reviewing PRs: English only; call out wrong base, empty template, and security issues as blocking.
- Do not add AI co-author trailers (`Co-authored-by:`) unless the human explicitly asks.
